  "body": "First batch from a full mobile audit (every tab measured at 375px). Focuses on the data-entry flow, which was built desktop-first.\n\n## Changes\n- **Numeric keypads for weight/reps/sets** — these inputs were `type=\"text\"`, so phones showed the full QWERTY keyboard. Added `inputMode=\"decimal\"` (weight) / `inputMode=\"numeric\"` (reps/sets) and bumped touch height (`py-2` → `py-3`). ([WorkoutDrawer.jsx](frontend/src/components/WorkoutDrawer.jsx))\n- **Log tab in the mobile bottom nav** — it was missing entirely (reachable only via the hamburger). Now surfaced **centered** as the primary daily action for admins; public visitors still see the same four tabs. ([App.jsx](frontend/src/App.jsx))\n- **Safe-area handling** — added `viewport-fit=cover` + `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` padding so the bottom nav isn't tucked under the home indicator on notched phones, and padded the scroll area so the last content row clears the fixed nav.\n\n## Audit context (no code changes needed, but noted)\nMeasured at 375px: **no horizontal overflow on any tab** — good baseline. Remaining item for a follow-up PR: touch targets below the 44px guideline across the app (hamburger 32px, filter chips 30px, Exercises day buttons 34px, History controls 26–36px, Today exercise links 24px).\n\n## Verification\nBuilt + linted (0 errors). Verified live at 375px: bottom nav renders correctly, content clears the nav (76px + safe area). Weight/reps/sets `inputMode` confirmed in source (those inputs render after marking an exercise done, which needs auth — will eyeball on-device after deploy).",
